$$
\dfrac{4}{\sqrt{24}} = \dfrac{4}{2\sqrt{6}} = \dfrac{2}{\sqrt{6}}
$$

We rationalize the denominator:

$$
\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{6}} = \dfrac{2 \cdot \sqrt{6}}{6} = \dfrac{\sqrt{6}}{3}
$$

**Term 2**: $\dfrac{\sqrt{3456}}{9}$

First, factor 3456:

$$
