$$
\frac{2}{3} \cdot 5 < x < \frac{6}{7} \cdot 5
$$
$$
\frac{10}{3} < x < \frac{30}{7}
$$

---

### Step 2: Convert the fractions to decimal form
$$
\frac{10}{3} \approx 3.3333 \quad \text{and} \quad \frac{30}{7} \approx 4.2857
$$

Therefore, the inequality becomes:
$$
3.3333 < x < 4.2857
$$

---

### Step 3: Find integer values satisfying this inequality
The only integer between 3.3333 and 4.2857 is $x = 4$.

