$$

Similarly, the number of ways to choose 2 girls from 4 is:

$$
C(4, 2) = \frac{4!}{2!(4-2)!} = \frac{4 \times 3}{2 \times 1} = 6
$$

The total number of ways to select 3 boys and 2 girls is the product of these two combinations:

$$
35 \times 6 = 210
$$

